# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Font binaries. `* text=auto` above detects these as binary by the NUL bytes
# they contain, but saying so outright means a font that happens not to is
# still never line-ending-normalised on checkout. A mangled .ttf renders as
# nothing; app/test/features/fonts_test.dart checks the version tag for the
# same reason.
*.ttf binary

# The medicines bundle (ADR-0013), compressed with zlib. Same reasoning as the
# fonts: a chunk without a NUL byte early on would otherwise be taken for text,
# and a chunk with its line endings rewritten no longer decompresses.
*.zlib binary

# Generated data whose exact bytes are pinned by a SHA-256 in generated Dart:
# the priors artifact (priors_bundled.dart), the herbal supplements asset
# (supplements_bundled.dart), and the medicines selection and groups that
# gen_medicines.py and gen_medicine_groups.py check the same way.
#
# `* text=auto` above gives these CRLF on a Windows checkout, which changes
# every byte after a newline and so changes the hash. The generators compute it
# over the file as they wrote it, with LF, so the checked-out file hashes to
# something else and priors_test and supplements_test fail on a developer's
# machine while passing in CI. Pinning the checkout to LF makes the hash mean
# the same thing on every platform.
artifacts/**/*.json text eol=lf
app/assets/**/*.json text eol=lf
